{
  "id": "bigville_craft",
  "version": "2.3.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R57 (block 370000): TOOLS ARE ASSEMBLED FROM PARTS MADE BY DIFFERENT CRAFTSMEN. A pick is not made by the smith alone -- it is a HEAD (forged by the BLACKSMITH from iron) fitted to a HANDLE (carved by the WOODWORKER from timber). cr_forge_head / cr_carve_handle each mint a Component whose quality = that craftsman's skill; a lone part gets only a WEAK improvised Fitness (IMPROV=0.2 of full) -- 'alone they are not hugely useful'. cr_assemble fits a loose head + loose handle into a working Tool: it takes the head's identity (kind/verb/base_mult), its QUALITY is the average of the two parts (a poor handle spoils a good head), and its Fitness = base_mult*combined -- FAR above either part alone. The parts are CONSUMED into the tool (part_of). Closes two loops (ore->iron->head, timber->handle) and needs TWO trades to cooperate. The tool is a bigville_tools Tool (fit_for -> Fitness{verb,mult,effort}), immediately usable. Composes with bigville_tools, mining/woodcutting (materials), bigville_office (the two trades), the market. CHARCOAL: the forge burns CHARCOAL (store.charcoal), not raw wood; the COLLIER (cc_burn) makes charcoal from wood with a ~0.25 yield -- closing woodcutter->timber->collier->charcoal->forge.",
