      "batch": false,
      "comment": "A BLACKSMITH forges a HEAD (the working iron -- a pick-head, an axe-head, a scythe-blade) from IRON + fuel. The head carries the tool's IDENTITY: its kind, its verb (mine/reap/...), its base_mult. Alone it is only weakly useful (an improvised Fitness at IMPROV of full). FUEL IS CHARCOAL: the forge burns store.charcoal (not raw wood -- wood won't reach forging heat); no charcoal -> no forging. (Composite orders only: making_simple==0, the default.)",
